ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Older adults (≥ 65 years)\n-  Subject has lower appendicular muscle mass index (AMMI) (<7 kg/m^2 in men; <5.7 kg/m^2 in women) using Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA, TANITA BC-418®, Tokyo, Japan)\n-  Subject has lower handgrip strength (<26 kg in men; <18 kg in women) using dynamometer (CAMRY®, Zhongshan, Guangdong) or slowly gait speed (<1 m/s)\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "raw_text": "- Older adults (≥ 65 years)",\n          "Eq-Operator": [\n            "≥"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n            "years"\n          ],\n          "Age": [\n            "Older adults"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Value": [\n            "65"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "≥ 65 years"\n          ]\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "- Subject has lower appendicular muscle mass index (AMMI) (<7 kg/m^2 in men; <5.7 kg/m^2 in women) using Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA, TANITA BC-418®, Tokyo, Japan)",\n          "Observation": [\n            "appendicular muscle mass index",\n            "AMMI"\n          ],\n          "Observation-Name": [\n            "appendicular muscle mass index",\n            "AMMI"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Operator": [\n            "<"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Unit": [\n            "kg",\n            "m^2"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Value": [\n            "7",\n            "5.7"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "<7 kg/m^2",\n            "<5.7 kg/m^2"\n     