ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Patients and parents of the patients who accept to participate and sign the informed consent\n-  Patients whose molar teeth are diagnosed as molar incisor hypomineralization by EAPD\n-  Teeth that are fully erupted\n-  Patients who have at least two permanent first molars that need fissure sealant\n-  Teeth that have white-yellow-brown discoloration that indicate high-caries risk\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Patients and parents of the patients who accept to participate and sign the informed consent"\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Patients whose molar teeth are diagnosed as molar incisor hypomineralization by EAPD",\n                  "Condition": [\n                    "molar incisor hypomineralization"\n                  ],\n                  "Condition-Name": [\n                    "molar incisor hypomineralization"\n                  ],\n                  "Modifier": [\n                    "molar teeth"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "EAPD"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                    "EAPD"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Teeth that are fully erupted",\n              "Condition": [\n                "fully erupted"\n            