ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\nPregnant women in third trimester planned to undergo elective cesarean section\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "Pregnant women",\n      "Condition": [\n        "Pregnant"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "Pregnant"\n      ],\n      "Life-Stage-And-Gender": [\n        "women"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "in third trimester planned to undergo elective cesarean section",\n      "Procedure": [\n        "cesarean section"\n      ],\n      "Procedure-Name": [\n        "cesarean section"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Comparison": [\n        "third trimester"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Value": [\n        "third"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n        "trimester"\n      ],\n      "Modifier": [\n        "elective"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n        "planned to undergo"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
