ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  The exclusion criteria were pregnancy, presence of a urinary tract infection and previous treatment for SI. The removal criteria were patient non-compliance with the protocol, failure in contacting the patient and the patient\'s wish to withdraw from the study.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "- The exclusion criteria were pregnancy, presence of a urinary tract infection",\n      "Condition": [\n        "pregnancy",\n        "urinary tract infection"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "pregnancy",\n        "urinary tract infection"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "OR": {\n        "left": {\n          "raw_text": "and previous treatment for SI. The removal criteria were patient non-compliance with the protocol, failure in contacting the patient",\n          "Procedure": [\n            "treatment"\n          ],\n          "Condition": [\n            "SI"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "previous"\n          ],\n          "Condition-Name": [\n            "SI"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n            "previous"\n          ]\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "and the patient\'s wish to withdraw from the study.",\n          "Study": [\n            "study"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
